# Story: someone in a video call all day pins the call, then works as usual: frames the editor, walks to
# the browser, clicks around, arranges, floats everything, pauses. The call never leaves the view, is never
# covered, and never takes the keyboard by itself.
# Reference: F49 (A-items in collab/parity.json). Window ids start at 101.
open Editor
open Browser
open Zoom 320x240
move 103 1090 50 320 240
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
# Without a pin the call leaves with the Desktop.
zoom 101
expect hidden 103
show-all
expect visible 103
# Keep "Zoom" in View.
move 103 1090 50 320 240
pin 103
expect ok
expect pinned 103
expect floating 103
focus 101
zoom
expect fills 101
expect visible 103
expect in-front 103
neighbor right
expect camera desktop
expect visible 103
neighbor right
expect fills 102
expect visible 103
expect in-front 103
# Clicking the window under it does not bury it.
focus 102
expect in-front 103
show-all
expect visible 103
# Dragging moves it, even over the edge of a docked window, where any other window would dock.
drag 103 60 400 cmd
expect floating 103
expect pinned 103
move 103 1090 50 320 240
# Arranging leaves it out; floating everything leaves it where it is.
arrange
expect count docked 2
expect pinned 103
zoom 101
float-all
expect visible 103
expect pinned 103
# A pause lets go of everything and forgets nothing.
dock 101 left
zoom 101
pause
expect visible 103
resume
expect pinned 103
expect visible 103
# Docking it ends the pin, and floating it again does not bring the pin back.
show-all
dock 103 right
expect docked 103
float 103
pin 103
expect ok
unpin 103
expect ok
unpin 103
expect fail
# A rule pins the next call as it opens, whatever is in view.
rule com.example.facetime pin
zoom 101
open FaceTime 300x200
expect pinned 104
neighbor right
expect visible 104
